1
00:00:01,180 --> 00:00:03,377
Could this have happened
while we were sleeping?

2
00:00:03,460 --> 00:00:04,600
To me and Giorno?

3
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:06,040
Mista and Trish?

4
00:00:06,440 --> 00:00:08,877
What kind of messed up
voodoo crap is this?

5
00:00:08,960 --> 00:00:12,372
Last I checked, people's minds
couldn't just trade bodies?

6
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:15,840
Stay your hands for now!

7
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:18,560
Wait, that can't be a stand!

8
00:00:18,880 --> 00:00:19,939
Is that Zipperman?

9
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:21,440
Ain't no doubt!

10
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:23,960
It's Bucciarati!

11
00:00:30,840 --> 00:00:31,677
In my eyes,

12
00:00:31,760 --> 00:00:38,237
I'm going to turn back on my head.

13
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:39,150
I'm going

14
00:00:39,233 --> 00:00:45,880
to

15
00:00:57,100 --> 00:00:58,500
turn back on my head.

16
00:01:32,100 --> 00:01:35,840
Nessun può Star un destino scelto,

17
00:01:36,280 --> 00:01:41,080
Roman solo il risultato,
che voi sarete distrutti.

18
00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:47,257
L 'eterna Zoom esiste solo per me,

19
00:01:47,340 --> 00:01:51,940
puoi cantare canzoni di
trastezza nel Monday senza tempo.

20
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:27,440
Oh, thank God!

21
00:02:27,720 --> 00:02:28,997
Glad to have you back!

22
00:02:29,080 --> 00:02:32,786
You even beat the boss to the
punch and tracked down the arrow!

23
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:34,780
I know that cadence.

24
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:38,097
That's how Narancia
speaks, if memory serves.

25
00:02:38,180 --> 00:02:39,020
Am I right?

26
00:02:41,040 --> 00:02:41,960
Huh? Yeah!

27
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:45,200
Thought so. And you two?

28
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:47,520
I'm Giorno.

29
00:02:48,360 --> 00:02:49,540
And I'm Trish.

30
00:02:49,780 --> 00:02:51,580
Impressive work, Bucciarati.

31
00:02:51,940 --> 00:02:55,234
It appears you've already
pieced together what happened.

32
00:02:55,540 --> 00:02:56,817
Wait a minute...

33
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:59,606
Are you the man we were
supposed to meet with?

34
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:02,540
I am Jean-Pierre Polnareff.

35
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:06,080
I died by Diavolo's hand.

36
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:11,584
However, after switching
souls with this turtle,

37
00:03:11,760 --> 00:03:13,957
I was able to maintain a presence here?

38
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:16,477
like a ghost might haunt
the plane of the living.

39
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:18,880
And that over there is my stand.

40
00:03:19,540 --> 00:03:23,500
With the Eros' power, he was
transformed into Chariot Requiem.

41
00:03:23,940 --> 00:03:26,720
He is responsible for our displaced souls.

42
00:03:28,220 --> 00:03:29,050
Wait,

43
00:03:29,133 --> 00:03:33,617
if my soul's in this body, then it's only
natural to conclude the boss is inside.

44
00:03:33,700 --> 00:03:35,557
Yeah, don't worry about
him, he hasn't moved at all.

45
00:03:35,640 --> 00:03:37,228
Guy's sleeping like a baby.

46
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:39,200
Might you be, Mista?

47
00:03:40,180 --> 00:03:43,239
Yeah, I'm really glad to
see you're okay, old buddy.

48
00:03:44,340 --> 00:03:46,417
Anyway, number seven's
got his eye on your body.

49
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:49,559
If it's so much as twitches,
we'll know immediately.

50
00:03:49,780 --> 00:03:51,020
Again, he's out cold.

51
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:53,459
Might be a while before he gets up.

52
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:55,630
Bucciarati!

53
00:03:55,713 --> 00:03:57,319
Chariot Requiem's back on his feet!

54
00:03:59,080 --> 00:04:01,257
We've already learned
how to use the arrow.

55
00:04:01,340 --> 00:04:04,520
If we can just grab it,
this'll all be over!

56
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:22,080
What's this, Zippermann?

57
00:04:22,300 --> 00:04:23,620
What are you doing?

58
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:26,600
Quick, the arrow!

59
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:28,520
Requiem's going for it!

60
00:04:36,520 --> 00:04:38,660
Not on my watch, you little bitch.

61
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:40,760
No, wait, something's wrong.

62
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:42,980
Miseria, did he?

63
00:04:48,160 --> 00:04:50,177
I'm gonna kill you, you stupid ass!

64
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:53,857
That thick skull of yours is about to
become holier than a dog shit-eating priest!

65
00:04:53,940 --> 00:04:56,400
The pillar next to you! Mesa! Doc!

66
00:04:58,460 --> 00:04:59,340
Spicy lady!

67
00:05:03,420 --> 00:05:04,620
Die, you bastard!

68
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:07,477
I'm gonna blast your
ugly head open and paint

69
00:05:07,560 --> 00:05:10,089
the streets with your
chunky noodle juices!

70
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:12,300
You'll number one cut the shit out!

71
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:14,817
What the hell do you think
you're doing, you moron?

72
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:15,900
Hey, stop it!

73
00:05:17,260 --> 00:05:18,090
Huh?

74
00:05:19,460 --> 00:05:20,660
What was I doing?

75
00:05:21,080 --> 00:05:21,960
What happened?

76
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:23,100
It can't be!

77
00:05:25,140 --> 00:05:26,420
Guys! Over there!

78
00:05:27,140 --> 00:05:27,970
Requiem!

79
00:05:28,053 --> 00:05:29,217
He's going for the arrow!

80
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:31,065
We can't just let him take it!

81
00:05:39,760 --> 00:05:41,940
Oh, you gotta be freaking kidding me!

82
00:05:42,060 --> 00:05:43,517
How did all that just happen?

83
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:44,718
If I were to guess,

84
00:05:45,440 --> 00:05:47,558
It's a result of his frenetic state.

85
00:05:47,840 --> 00:05:51,700
Not even I have seen chariots show
such terrifying powers before.

86
00:05:52,540 --> 00:05:54,080
But this much is clear.

87
00:05:54,380 --> 00:05:58,520
In response to my subconscious
will, he's become a defensive stand.

88
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:02,471
As long as he lives, he'll
allow no one to touch the arrow.

89
00:06:02,660 --> 00:06:04,860
To turn stands against their users.

90
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:08,557
Such a cunning defense mechanism
will prove challenging to defeat.

91
00:06:08,640 --> 00:06:13,157
So not only can the arrow control all
our minds, it can pull tricks like this?

92
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:15,181
How are we supposed to get at it?

93
00:06:15,320 --> 00:06:16,673
Dude is out of control!

94
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:18,630
Sure,

95
00:06:18,713 --> 00:06:20,057
our stands might be supercharged,

96
00:06:20,140 --> 00:06:25,022
but that just means if we try to grab the
arrow right now, we'll get roasted alive!

97
00:06:30,840 --> 00:06:31,670
Bad Benedict!

98
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:33,780
No howling! You pipe down!

99
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:37,980
Oh, there, there.

100
00:06:38,260 --> 00:06:39,200
It'll be okay.

101
00:06:44,760 --> 00:06:45,800
Hey, Mista!

102
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:49,002
Something's making number
seven lose his barbles!

103
00:06:49,820 --> 00:06:52,840
Whoever's inside, Bucciarati,
they're coming too!

104
00:06:54,240 --> 00:06:56,200
My god, is it him?

105
00:06:56,340 --> 00:06:58,077
We can worry about the arrow later.

106
00:06:58,160 --> 00:07:00,984
Get into place and don't
take your eyes off him!

107
00:07:02,800 --> 00:07:05,271
Now, Mista, take a shot and make it count!

108
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:08,760
What did I say?

109
00:07:08,960 --> 00:07:10,477
Put those bullets of yours to work!

110
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:11,660
Yeah, I heard.

111
00:07:11,860 --> 00:07:15,317
But, dude, did you forget that's
your body I'd be shooting at?

112
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:16,871
There's no need to worry.

113
00:07:17,300 --> 00:07:20,437
Golden Wind can patch up
bullet wounds without effort.

114
00:07:20,520 --> 00:07:21,350
So, shoot.

115
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:23,678
All we gotta do is incapacitate him.

116
00:07:24,540 --> 00:07:26,658
That was your plan, right, Bucerati?

117
00:07:29,800 --> 00:07:31,180
Guys, he's on the move!

118
00:07:31,340 --> 00:07:32,693
Come on, let's get him!

119
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:39,977
That should do it, fellas!

120
00:07:40,060 --> 00:07:43,119
I don't think he'll be
charging at us any time soon!

121
00:07:46,820 --> 00:07:48,702
No one's showing up on my radar!

122
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:51,981
Looks like there won't be
any backup to deal with.

123
00:07:54,860 --> 00:07:55,780
We did it!

124
00:07:58,160 --> 00:08:01,000
Once we get the arrow,
this'll all be over.

125
00:08:03,080 --> 00:08:06,380
And then, when we're back in
Napoli, it's off to school.

126
00:08:07,100 --> 00:08:08,757
Hot damn, I'm already psyched.

127
00:08:08,840 --> 00:08:12,797
The first thing I'll do is stuff my
face with an authentic margarita slice.

128
00:08:12,880 --> 00:08:14,821
Might even top it with porcini's.

129
00:08:15,280 --> 00:08:16,460
After that...

130
00:08:18,340 --> 00:08:22,880
If I ever see Fugo again, he can
call me a kagakatsu all he wants.

131
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:24,780
I won't give two shits.

132
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:28,820
And even though Bakio's gone...

133
00:08:35,140 --> 00:08:35,970
Trish!

134
00:08:36,053 --> 00:08:37,855
I'll protect you till my dying breath!

135
00:08:38,040 --> 00:08:39,040
That's a promise!

136
00:08:41,620 --> 00:08:42,450
Narancia...

137
00:08:42,533 --> 00:08:45,940
Mista, just to be safe,
take out both of his legs.

138
00:08:46,720 --> 00:08:47,602
Uh, yeah, sure.

139
00:08:47,860 --> 00:08:50,417
Hey Trish, would you mind
handing me my bullets?

140
00:08:50,500 --> 00:08:51,397
I want them all.

141
00:08:51,480 --> 00:08:53,597
Just reach down into
my boot and grab them.

142
00:08:53,680 --> 00:08:54,900
Uh, okay. Okay.

143
00:09:01,440 --> 00:09:03,197
Hey, pick up the pace, will ya?

144
00:09:03,280 --> 00:09:04,877
Those legs won't shoot themselves.

145
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:06,300
Wait, hold on a sec.

146
00:09:17,060 --> 00:09:18,520
Time jumped, just now.

147
00:09:18,720 --> 00:09:20,077
We skipped a few seconds.

148
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:22,337
I know, the bullets
that fell on the ground.

149
00:09:22,420 --> 00:09:24,077
Did anyone actually hear them land?

150
00:09:24,160 --> 00:09:25,020
It can't be.

151
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:26,697
I was watching him closely.

152
00:09:26,780 --> 00:09:30,337
Not once did I catch him move,
let alone evoke Emperor Crimson.

153
00:09:30,420 --> 00:09:32,260
It just doesn't make any sense.

154
00:09:32,540 --> 00:09:36,540
What other nefarious forces could
possibly be haunting us this time?

155
00:09:38,040 --> 00:09:38,870
Listen, Trish.

156
00:09:38,953 --> 00:09:40,547
I might need a little favor.

157
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:44,000
Could you go ahead and drop
one more bullet for me?

158
00:09:44,880 --> 00:09:46,440
Oh, come on! Are you deaf?

159
00:09:46,620 --> 00:09:49,817
Can you even count how many of them
are rolling around there right now?

160
00:09:49,900 --> 00:09:51,020
The answer's four!

161
00:09:51,180 --> 00:09:52,397
The absolute freaking worst!

162
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:55,257
I can't have that bullshit
number anywhere near me!

163
00:09:55,340 --> 00:09:57,317
If they fell while you
were handing them over,

164
00:09:57,400 --> 00:10:00,988
then for the love of God, do me
a solid and drop another one!

165
00:10:01,640 --> 00:10:03,100
How sure are we exactly?

166
00:10:03,300 --> 00:10:04,712
That's Diavolo in there.

167
00:10:05,700 --> 00:10:08,180
Hey Trish, could you just remind me again?

168
00:10:08,380 --> 00:10:11,557
When we all woke up, you said you
couldn't sense the boss anywhere,

169
00:10:11,640 --> 00:10:12,640
isn't that right?

170
00:10:13,520 --> 00:10:14,657
Well, what about now?

171
00:10:14,740 --> 00:10:16,799
Are you picking up anything at all?

172
00:10:18,600 --> 00:10:20,097
That cannot be the case!

173
00:10:20,180 --> 00:10:24,180
You swapped with Narancia, and
accordingly Mista swapped with Trish.

174
00:10:24,520 --> 00:10:27,461
It stands to reason Buterati
swapped with Diavolo.

175
00:10:27,560 --> 00:10:30,277
With Requiem's powers, they're
the only pairings that work.

176
00:10:30,360 --> 00:10:34,177
Yeah, I get what you're saying, but none
of that explains why time just jumped.

177
00:10:34,260 --> 00:10:38,848
That can only mean whoever's in that
body right now can't possibly be Diavolo.

178
00:10:39,340 --> 00:10:41,557
Narancia, how does our perimeter look?

179
00:10:41,640 --> 00:10:43,816
Are you able to detect anyone coming?

180
00:10:50,300 --> 00:10:51,130
Narancia?

181
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:07,800
Please, I'm begging you.

182
00:11:09,980 --> 00:11:12,777
Just one more bullet,
please just drop one more.

183
00:11:12,860 --> 00:11:13,690
You're driving me back.

184
00:11:13,773 --> 00:11:14,603
What the hell?

185
00:11:14,686 --> 00:11:17,077
Why couldn't I feel a
soul like I usually do?

186
00:11:17,160 --> 00:11:18,689
It doesn't make any sense.

187
00:11:19,440 --> 00:11:20,780
Out of the way! Move!

188
00:11:21,160 --> 00:11:22,860
Let me through! Now!

189
00:11:23,560 --> 00:11:24,390
Dammit, no!

190
00:11:24,500 --> 00:11:25,559
That's impossible!

191
00:11:25,660 --> 00:11:26,957
How on earth could he have?

192
00:11:27,040 --> 00:11:28,880
Match, scan the area right now!

193
00:11:29,100 --> 00:11:30,982
Make sure there's no one around!

194
00:11:35,300 --> 00:11:36,130
Narancia!

195
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:39,030
Butcherati!

196
00:11:39,113 --> 00:11:40,717
Hurry up and get him down from there!

197
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:42,197
Don't just leave him like that!

198
00:11:42,280 --> 00:11:43,237
Do something, goddammit!

199
00:11:43,320 --> 00:11:44,457
You need to settle down!

200
00:11:44,540 --> 00:11:45,477
Let me handle this!

201
00:11:45,560 --> 00:11:47,577
Please stay focused and
keep your gun at the ready!

202
00:11:47,660 --> 00:11:48,780
He'll attack again.

203
00:11:49,020 --> 00:11:51,491
We have to find him before he does, quick!

204
00:11:55,160 --> 00:11:56,120
Go, Zipperman!

205
00:12:00,660 --> 00:12:01,490
Heal him!

206
00:12:01,760 --> 00:12:04,878
Pull those jam bars out of
there and get to work now!

207
00:12:11,160 --> 00:12:13,866
The people outside the
Coliseum are waking up.

208
00:12:14,200 --> 00:12:15,260
So where is he?

209
00:12:15,480 --> 00:12:16,757
I can't sense him at all.

210
00:12:16,840 --> 00:12:18,016
It's like he's gone.

211
00:12:18,820 --> 00:12:20,577
What else could have happened?

212
00:12:20,660 --> 00:12:24,013
There's no way in hell he'd
just up and vanish like that.

213
00:12:24,500 --> 00:12:27,735
Emperor Crimson's range is
two or three meters at most.

214
00:12:28,060 --> 00:12:30,766
How then did he attack
us from way over there?

215
00:12:33,720 --> 00:12:35,640
Well, all right. You did it.

216
00:12:35,980 --> 00:12:36,862
Naraj is awake.

217
00:12:37,620 --> 00:12:39,561
Welcome back, you little bastard.

218
00:12:39,880 --> 00:12:41,056
How are you feeling?

219
00:12:41,480 --> 00:12:43,420
Jeez, you really scared us.

220
00:12:44,280 --> 00:12:45,340
I'm sorry, Nista.

221
00:12:46,840 --> 00:12:50,680
There's no one left in here.

222
00:12:52,900 --> 00:12:54,240
It's empty.

223
00:12:55,260 --> 00:12:57,848
The physical wounds he
suffered have healed.

224
00:12:58,520 --> 00:13:01,520
But still, Golden Wind
couldn't get to him in time.

225
00:13:02,280 --> 00:13:03,180
He was...

226
00:13:03,700 --> 00:13:04,980
He was already gone.

227
00:13:06,860 --> 00:13:09,097
But I'm just...

228
00:13:09,180 --> 00:13:10,360
Not here.

229
00:13:15,620 --> 00:13:20,017
His form it's just an
empty vessel now I can't

230
00:13:20,100 --> 00:13:25,200
find him his soul has
left there's nothing here?

231
00:13:25,940 --> 00:13:30,137
Try as I might I can't
bring him back I wasn't

232
00:13:30,220 --> 00:13:33,077
fast enough my soul could
just slip right back

233
00:13:33,160 --> 00:13:35,677
in if it wanted it could
inhabit both bodies

234
00:13:35,760 --> 00:13:39,640
without a problem not
even one he's that empty.

235
00:13:55,260 --> 00:13:57,340
It was all so sudden.

236
00:13:57,760 --> 00:13:59,525
None of us could have guessed.

237
00:14:09,640 --> 00:14:11,000
No!

238
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:09,457
That bastard, where could he be hiding?

239
00:15:09,540 --> 00:15:11,422
This should never have happened.

240
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:15,340
The only explanation is if
there were two Diavolos.

241
00:15:16,940 --> 00:15:19,940
Wait, the child that appeared before him.

242
00:15:20,560 --> 00:15:21,680
Could it be?

243
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:27,280
Were both of them one physical
body with two different souls?

244
00:15:30,100 --> 00:15:31,980
Butcherati, I got it.

245
00:15:32,340 --> 00:15:34,458
Diavolo must have two personalities.

246
00:15:34,580 --> 00:15:36,521
That is the only possible answer.

247
00:15:37,640 --> 00:15:41,522
The one currently inside your body
is the young man I met earlier.

248
00:15:41,820 --> 00:15:45,996
He and Diavolo may share a physical
body, but their souls are separate.

249
00:15:47,340 --> 00:15:50,440
The human soul can be a
strange and delicate thing.

250
00:15:50,760 --> 00:15:53,697
A traumatic childhood event
can easily fissure it.

251
00:15:53,780 --> 00:15:58,660
As the individual grows, so too do
the fissures until the soul is split.

252
00:15:59,880 --> 00:16:00,820
Over time,

253
00:16:01,040 --> 00:16:04,177
the second personality distinguishes
itself from the original,

254
00:16:04,260 --> 00:16:06,613
with one of them soon becoming dominant.

255
00:16:06,980 --> 00:16:09,080
It's a well-documented disorder.

256
00:16:10,580 --> 00:16:11,600
Listen to me.

257
00:16:11,820 --> 00:16:14,180
What I'm saying is no mere conjecture.

258
00:16:14,760 --> 00:16:17,037
Reports from across Europe
confirm that even one's

259
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:20,473
physical form will change as
